@namespace NoBorders.Components.Screens
@using NoBorders.Services
@inject AppStateService State
@* Stub per Phase 2.6's scope ("stub views for Permissions/About") — the
   design bundle has no dedicated mockup for this nav item, but the
   underlying feature is real and already shown in the current WinForms
   Settings tab (CheckElevation/RestartAsAdmin), so this reuses that exact
   content restyled with the new tokens rather than a blank placeholder.
   design-handoff's 1g elevation-dialog icon treatment (amber warning
   square) is reused here for the same "needs elevation" concept.

   Phase 8.4 bugfix: wired to real data — State.IsElevated (MainForm's
   `_isElevated`, set once by CheckElevation() at startup) drives the status
   line and whether the button/hint show at all (nothing to do if already
   elevated, mirroring the WinForms tab's own `_btnRestartAdmin.Visible =
   !_isElevated`). The button previously had no @onclick at all — clicking
   it silently did nothing. It now calls State.ConfirmAndRestartAsAdmin(),
   which shows the same native confirmation MessageBox the WinForms tab's
   button always has before actually restarting. *@

<div class="nb-permissions-page__title">Permissions</div>

<div class="nb-permissions-page__status">
    <span class="nb-permissions-page__status-ring @(State.IsElevated ? "nb-permissions-page__status-ring--elevated" : "")"></span>
    <span>@(State.IsElevated ? "Running as Administrator" : "Running as Standard User")</span>
</div>

@if (!State.IsElevated)
{
    <button type="button" class="nb-btn nb-btn--outline nb-permissions-page__restart" @onclick="() => State.ConfirmAndRestartAsAdmin()">Restart as Administrator</button>

    <div class="nb-permissions-page__hint">
        Only needed if a tracked game isn't going borderless and you see an elevation warning.
    </div>
}
